+++++++++++ Optional Using Ngnix as a Reverse Proxy for AdGuard +++++++++++++

in this optional you can also use what i called NPM nginx proxy manager 

follow this link <>  to know how to setup NPM 

But here i will be using Nginx a as Reverse Proxy 

First edit your docker file in the port section

Now let your AdGuard port run on 8080 

Here make sure you have nginx running on your ubuntu server on port 80 

<check this link>   how to install nginx proxy

if nginx is running and up 

sudo systemctl start nginx 

sudo systemctl status nginx 

after nginx running then edit adguard DOCKER file 

    ports:
      - "53:53/tcp"
      - "53:53/udp"
      - "8080:80/tcp"    # Web interface
      - "3000:3000/tcp"  # Initial setup port (optional)

after use docker compose up 

then try access URL of adGuard <http://<Your_Ubuntu_SERVER_IP>:8080>

then edit the Nginx config file by adding this 

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name adguard.example.com;        # change this (ubuntu_server_ip)

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}


After reload nginx app

sudo systemctl reload nginx 

then after you can access AdGuard URL 

just http://<ubuntu_server_ip>      or if you have custome name example adguard-aka-tech-it.info

if you encounter any problem mostly will be port issues just search online how to solve it. 

